AB  -  Purpose: The benefit of adjuvant chemotherapy after resection of pancreatic cancer following neoadjuvant FOLFIRINOX (folinic acid, 5‐fluorouracil, irinotecan, and oxaliplatin) is unclear. This international study aimed to assess the treatment effect of adjuvant chemotherapy on overall survival (OS) in different subgroups of patients after resection of pancreatic cancer following neoadjuvant FOLFIRINOX. Materials and methods: Retrospective, international, multicenter cohort study including patients after resection of pancreatic cancer following neoadjuvant FOLFIRINOX (2012‐2018). The impact of adjuvant chemotherapy on OS was evaluated in different subgroups including interaction terms for clinicopathological parameters with adjuvant treatment in a multivariable Cox model. Results: We included 520 patients from 31 centers in 19 countries. The median number of neoadjuvant cycles FOLFIRINOX was 6 (IQR 5‐8). Overall, 343 patients (66%) received adjuvant chemotherapy, of which 68 (20%) (m)FOLFIRINOX, 201 (59%) gemcitabine‐based chemotherapy, and 74 (22%) a combination/other. Median OS was 38 months after diagnosis. No survival difference was found for patients who received adjuvant chemotherapy versus those who did not (median OS 38 vs. 40 months, log‐rank p=0.94; Figure 1). In multivariable analysis, only the interaction term for N‐stage with adjuvant therapy was significant (p=0.006). In node‐positive patients, the median OS was 36 months with and 21 months without adjuvant therapy (log‐rank p<0.001; multivariable HR 0.43; 95% CI 0.23‐0.78; Figure 2). In node‐negative patients, the median OS was 51 months with and 65 months without adjuvant therapy (log‐rank p=0.11, multivariable HR 0.92; 95% CI 0.37‐2.27; Figure 3). Conclusions: Adjuvant chemotherapy after neoadjuvant FOLFIRINOX and resection of pancreatic cancer was associated with improved survival in node‐positive, but not in node‐negative patients. This should be evaluated prospectively in a multicenter randomized trial. References [Formula presented] Overall survival of patients undergoing resection of pancreatic cancer following neoadjuvant FOLFIRINOX stratified by adjuvant therapy [Formula presented] Overall survival of patients after resection of pancreatic cancer with node‐positive (ypN+) disease stratified by adjuvant therapy [Formula presented] Overall survival of patients after resection of pancreatic caner with pathology proven node‐negative (ypN‐) disease stratified by adjuvant therapy The authors do not declare any conflict of interest
