DO  -  10.1016/S1879-4068(19)31139-7
AB  -  Introduction: Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) mainly occurs in older adult. Since randomized clinical trials (RCTs) provide the highest‐quality evidence incorporated in NCCN recommendations, the underrepresentation of elderly in RCTs challenges the external validity of guidelines and limits the solidity of evidence in this specific population. Objectives: The study aimed to investigate external validity of NCCN guidelines for PDCA in a real‐world older population (≥70 years old). Methods: We identified the following questions about PDAC management from NCCN guidelines: 1) adjuvant chemotherapy and 2) chemoradiation versus surgery alone; 3) neoadjuvant chemo/chemoradiation versus surgery alone; 4) chemoradiation versus chemotherapy and 5) best radiosensitizer chemotherapy in locally advanced PDAC. For each question we matched characteristics of patients with PDAC from Moffitt database with the reference RCTs eligibility criteria (EC) to check their qualification for at least 2 RCTs. Eligibility >60% was rated full validity, 30–60% partial validity, <30% limited validity (de Water, 2014). We also performed log‐rank test to assessed whether “eligibility” status affect OS, stratifying by age (70–74; 75–79; ≥80). Results and Conclusions: We retrospectively analyzed 707 subjects with PDAC, 70–93 years old and collected 95 RCTs from pancreatic NCCN guidelines. We found full validity for neoadjuvant (57/73 patients; 69.86%) and locally advanced (28/39; 71.79%) chemoradiotherapy, partial validity for adjuvant chemotherapy (37/86; 43.02%) and adjuvant chemoradiotherapy (19/35; 54.28%). Lowest validity was found for radiosensitizer chemotherapy (13/37; 35.13%). No differences were observed in age‐related subgroups. Main exclusion criteria were second malignancies, renal impairment, age >75, previous neoadjuvant therapy and time from surgery in adjuvant setting. Irrespective of age, eligible status was correlated with a significant OS benefit for question 4 (p=0.002). Although retrospective, our analysis supports the limitation of guidelines’ external validity in elderly and suggests its impact on survival. Renewing RCT design with broader EC might help increase inclusion of older and thus strengthen the evidence. Disclosure of interest: None declared
