y Questionnaire[At baseline, potential midpoint ( 4 months post‐intervention commencement), and at the completion of the intervention (maximum 6 months post‐intervention commencement)] Progression‐free survival as measured by the length of time elapsed between intervention initiation and tumour progression or death from any cause[At the potential midpoint ( 4 months post‐intervention commencement), the completion of the intervention (maximum 6 months post‐intervention commencement), and six months after the post‐intervention assessment] Psychological distress measured using the Brief Symptom Inventory‐18 questionnaire[At baseline, potential midpoint ( 4 months post‐intervention commencement), and at the completion of the intervention (maximum 6 months post‐intervention commencement)] Quality of life measured using the European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer Quality of Life Questionnaire Core module (EORTC QLQ‐C30) in conjunction with the disease‐specific module (EORTC QLQ‐PAN26)[At baseline, potential midpoint ( 4 months post‐intervention commencement), and at the completion of the intervention (maximum 6 months post‐intervention commencement)] R0 resection rate examined as the proportion of the study patients who undergo elective surgical resection with clear margin (defined as >1mm); the relevant data will be obtained from participants' medical records[At the potential midpoint ( 4 months post‐intervention commencement), and the completion of the intervention (maximum 6 months post‐intervention commencement)] Resumption of activities of daily living as measured by a modified Resumption of Activities of Daily Living Scale in patients who undergo elective surgery[At six months after the post‐intervention assessment (maximum 12 months post‐intervention commencement)] Surgical resection rate assessed as the proportion of the study patients who achieve resectability as defined by the Australiasian Gastro‐Intestinal Trials Group and who proceed to elective surgical resection; the relevant data will be obtained from participants' medical records[At the potential midpoint ( 4 months post‐intervention commencement), and the completion of the intervention (maximum 6 months post‐intervention commencement)] The views of participants towards the sport‐related component in the program as examined by the Physical Activity Enjoyment Scale (PACES)[At the completion of the intervention (maximum 6 months post‐intervention commencement)] Tumour progression measured using imaging scans (e.g., PET‐CT and MRI) and/or blood biomarkers (e.g., carbohydrate antigen 19‐9)[At the potential midpoint ( INCLUSION CRITERIA: Patients diagnosed with borderline resectable or locally advanced pancreatic adenocarcinoma as per the definition proposed by the Australasian Gastro‐Intestinal Trials Group and waiting to commence or within four weeks after starting their prescribed chemotherapy
