PY  -  2017
C3  -  CTgov NCT03038477
M3  -  Trial registry record
KW  -  Durvalumab
AB  -  Borderline resectable pancreatic cancer (BRPC) patients who have successfully underwent R0/R1 resection of PDAs following neoadjuvant chemotherapy, between 1‐3 months after the completion of planned adjuvant chemotherapy will be enrolled and randomized at a 1:1 ratio into two arms (56 per arm). Patients in Arm A will be given anti‐PD‐L1 antibody, durvalumab, every 2 weeks for a maximum of 26 doses if there is no radiographic evidence of disease recurrence. Patients in Arm B will be observed. Blood draws for immune monitoring and serum banking will be collected at the following time points: Arm A ‐ before Cycles 1, 2, 4, 7 and End of Treatment (EOT) visit; Arm B ‐ before Cycles 1, 4, 7, and End of Treatment (EOT) visit
