AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention1: D3 lymphadenectomy: D3 is Extended Lymphadenectomy The difference between a D3 and a D2 plus para‐aortic lymph node dissection is that in a D3, in addition to the lymph nodes removed at the time of a D2 lymphadenectomy, only some of the para aortic lymph nodes around the pancreas are removed. A complete clearance of the para aortic nodes, which is associated with the increased morbidity, is not performed in a D3 lymphadenectomy. Hence this avoids the increased morbidity encountered in the previous studies exploring the role of D2 plus para‐aortic lymph node dissection. Control Intervention1: D2 Lymphadenectomy: D2 Systematic Lymphadenectomy D2 lymphadenectomy that involves removal of up to the second echelon of draining lymph nodes The difference between a D3 and a D2 plus para‐aortic lymph node dissection is that in a D3, in addition to the lymph nodes removed at the time of a D2 lymphadenectomy, only some of the para aortic lymph nodes around the pancreas are removed. A complete clearance of the para aortic nodes, which is associated with the increased morbidity, is not performed in a D3 lymphadenectomy. Hence this avoids the increased morbidity encountered in the previous studies exploring the role of D2 plus para‐aortic lymph node dissection. CONDITION: Gastric Cancer PRIMARY OUTCOME: primary endpoint:Overall Survival ; ‐‐‐‐‐‐Timepoint: date of diagnosis to Date of death or last follow‐up SECONDARY OUTCOME: Disease‐free survival ; ‐‐‐‐‐‐Timepoint: date of diagnosis to date of death /recurrence INCLUSION CRITERIA: ‐ECOG performance status of 0 â?? 1 in patients deemed fit to undergo surgery at the pre‐anaesthetic check ‐Histologically proven gastric adenocarcinoma ‐No evidence of distant metastases, or locally advanced inoperable disease, as evaluated by computed tomography, chest radiography, ultrasonography, and / or laparotomy ‐Patient able to provide valid informed consent ‐Patient completed at least 1 cycle of neoadjuvant chemotherapy
